Pre-existing bug, NOT caused by NEARS-3088 (file not in this ticket's diff; unchanged since base
commit 6d005c4a0).

GET /admin/addon/system-addons (as authenticated admin) -> HTTP 500

storage/logs/laravel.log:
[2026-09-06 14:18:13] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Route [admin.system-addon.index] not defined.
{"correlation_id":"cf797cfd-838a-4bf7-acf2-746478058f93","type":"Symfony\\Component\\Routing\\Exception\\RouteNotFoundException","endpoint":"/admin/addon/system-addons"}

Root cause: routes/admin.php line ~244 has
    Route::get('addon/system-addons', function () {
        return to_route('admin.system-addon.index');
    })->name('addon.index');
but the real route (routes/admin.php ~line 534) is nested under a 'business-settings.' name
prefix, so its actual name is admin.business-settings.system-addon.index, not
admin.system-addon.index. The redirect closure calls the wrong route name and 500s. This closure
and the AddonController it targets are untouched by NEARS-3088's diff (24-file changeset does not
include routes/admin.php's addon.index closure or app/Http/Controllers/Admin/System/AddonController.php).
